      "name": "Giddy Iris Rhizome (Standard Dwarf Bearded)",
      "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">\"Giddy\" is the name of a&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?rlz=1CAVNCX_enUS1049US1049&amp;cs=0&amp;sca_esv=849bbf5d0204dfa6&amp;sxsrf=AE3TifMgauaiC9qblvcowZvjHwZV8GDLfA%3A1748281427807&amp;q=Standard+Dwarf+Bearded+Iris&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiypMXr18GNAxW8ATQIHQrcAUEQxccNegQIAhAB&amp;mstk=AUtExfCqkKZri4qyxdjEdFJL5zeBpGNd9e507a-toUfrXump_SZvt1wEyqYO5sBCzysLAnrc9iMid8PhJKCF6xNo-P24iP2EaPmKVY0GQiFere3NOIll3x7t5dN1ckBWmOPaiXdqC9ByuMzFsy6k1ntRZgs2Fwwqdzghb1P8xhF_atmJf5M&amp;csui=3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Standard Dwarf Bearded Iris</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">,&nbsp;a type of iris flower.&nbsp;This particular iris, developed by Johnson in 2011, is characterized by its&nbsp;dusty rose-pink color, with a violet flush up the midribs and a sweet fragrance.&nbsp;The falls (the drooping petal-like parts) have a white area around the large, fluffy, deep violet-blue beards.&nbsp;It is also known for its ability to form a great clump quickly.&nbsp;</span></p>",
